Etc29sLTIwMjYwOTI5fG9wZW5haSJ9","format":"openai-responses-v1","id":"rs_01f9d709b4551f68016af0ebcfb1bc87d1ab1d66373f1495a4","index":3},{"type":"reasoning.summary","summary":"**Exploring causal models**\n\nI'm thinking about how causal models can be tricky, especially with uncertain mechanisms. Even when the posterior remains the same across different actions, the outcomes still need to be recalculated. It’s interesting that we can’t just assume that causal consequences remain fixed. Then there's the question about referencing a future date—it shouldn't be a problem regarding revision 1381555528 since there's no specific date attached. There's definitely a lot to unpack here!","format":"openai-responses-v1","index":4},{"type":"reasoning.encrypted","data":"gAAAAABq8Ovnpvwgmhrbn4n2wyU66ydltsZ4hheZlk5knJfLus_hedYmH4ORNz0WUHKjgyguzIyqtT-XEcmjTF3-HPK7cjcEdtMCsKkKzhxBE-_msBm8ycc9nLkCFs7_XSa3qm3zyJzK24IAf3MHfkzkcBelObW2HKvRha2D8QWI3LXetSYrx__4MY_R0_avIxK8lj13ZpVcfS60q6ep31ZhMV7Qd3Qwwck0H-mKEadTpmSGTG2v8T5yCeztYiW-sYEpINpEoOl_v6N9uVEeP4XgnyEWCDhCC8HknjOE9-OV-GpsGBPATgboTXxGr1jrNhsnXcog5E8qyyoyzrC2tAqJuRrY4UIM1peYrwrTMHj0Owh5x812GUjC-xAs2uoan1-_v6hxqA0CyDoNwERkbdG3JApOGAHqtkok7fV1xZaiksyzy7lOKo10qhnwpXb9aJYmYIjlP916hOqlnX0ZKrd8zkrnZz0s1vmOwR9JUMlcmJqCRio8qM-HdBhPaF34q_cn9QQ6B_xue01Xk47BHZz_EPsFXeTkvHOAA7FVm_Bs7h1aZxHhMaagquLNXwMz2AWXyqh5eVbST0Ahp_X0srxTaqL5ogAdILLTWVS9CLRMTSuZgKTX2agB3rvjzOkITlyyExIXSDPHX6Qz8NJvMatGrd_sN1r5o4-6MVY2wUw4ZpLf4PmLrEFgGsyTUhJ3YKpptks4CAOeHfxrufQKLEIfQaQgvpNOi98sF5PW0H-9Gyea-X2tw78h0vpAUK_E2ufXoNCANiujSvaE2nvhmEqpbwgQS_9qtcQOrRadX0aBNQWsVnSwJtaIkKil1kFKkEGfdgNRz8j73cZA0z_ctqUB0s26sODQlYGX04K96Vz1I5mTcBFgw1P2itxIrEo0Z2W6ZFN3iGnGiqIJxLAUBMYdhs6rTdxyvjwkuPKQNDDeRbd4jijNN2FD55um8mRz9wGkGKLiqBDxlSifa01iupsQrFRJhHq5WNcX3mYuhNgsmOz2GFrv9bu7R6Aph0_MKvIySlLdyfTMQFhpFUbQFa2_HAPDhpakmWkp39oN9eH1UVRyJhfHhFHSAmTwL_rZO3LEvCCVTKEeK8k4eLrK0m02q4CD2kmjfmMjTF80sXRYjBhq_8DwKraXuLdHsQkWFG29ZwEOJrGBqNfrCPd3IxCALtqWUP1QBn3jfHLmHbSDgF_54hycaFMwA37huoR6D7Pu7Fgbc-0x4cO4ML6